      "extract": "The famous Atiyah-Singer index theorem \\cite{AS} relates the index of an elliptic pseudo-differential operator on a compact manifold $X$ to the Todd class of $X$ and the Chern character of the bundle naturally associated with the symbol of the pseudo-differential operator. It is well-known that the algebra of pseudo-differential operators can be viewed as a ``quantization'' of the cotangent bundle $T^{*}X$. Starting",
      "extractCut": true
    },
